MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
MCLENG counts the characters of its argument.
MCLENG(ABCDE) and MCLENG() and MCLENG(  two spaces  )
MCSUB takes a substring, counting from one.
MCSUB(ABC/XYZ,3,6)
MCSUB(ARGUMENT,-2,0)
MCSUB(ABCDE,1,1) and MCSUB(ABCDE,5,5)
An empty or impossible range gives nothing at all:
[MCSUB(ABCDE,4,2)] [MCSUB(ABCDE,0,9)] [MCSUB(ABCDE,2,99)]
The value is not evaluated again:
MCDEF ENT AS <SOMETHING ELSE>
[MCSUB(ARGUMENT,-2,0)]
